      "problem": "The center of the hyperbola $\\frac{{y}^{2}}{49}-\\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{81}=1$ is$\\,\\,($\n{{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}\n$).$",
      "worked_solution": "The equation of a vertical hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nNote that the given equation can be rewritten as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{7}^{2}}-\\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{{9}^{2}}=1\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have $h=3$ and $k=0.$\n\nTherefore, the center of the hyperbola is $(\\,3,0\\,).$",
